{
    "article_summary": "This article describes the development of dicyanopyrazine (DPZ)-derived push-pull chromophores as efficient organic photoredox catalysts. The study highlights DPZ derivative H, featuring a 2-methoxythienyl donor, which exhibits broad visible light absorption and excellent redox properties. These catalysts were successfully applied to cross-dehydrogenative-coupling (CDC) reactions, oxidative hydroxylation of aryl boronic acids, and reductive dehalogenation, achieving catalyst loadings as low as 0.01 mol%.",
